# After opening a pull request

Every time you open a PR (`gh pr create` or equivalent), immediately run the
setup script against the PR you just created, from the repo root:

```bash
.cursor/scripts/pr-setup.sh <pr-url>
```

The script assigns the pull request's author, adds the PR to the `Gamaliel Roadmap`
project (org `gamaliel-ai`, project number 1), sets Status to **In progress**,
sets Sprint to whichever iteration covers today, and sets **Project Start date**
to today. Today is the America/Los_Angeles calendar date. Cloud agents run in
UTC, so the UTC date is already the next day during the Pacific evening. The
author comes from `gh pr view <url> --json author`. The script does not assign
`@me` and does not hardcode a login.

When `GH_PROJECT_TOKEN` is set, the script passes it only to the pull request
read, the assignment, and the Roadmap project commands
(`GH_TOKEN="$GH_PROJECT_TOKEN" gh ...`). That value is a fine-grained token
owned by the `belovedbot` machine user, with Projects, Pull requests, and
Issues read/write on gamaliel-ai. It is not exported for the rest of the
script, and it is not used for reviews or approvals. If the pull request read,
the assignment, or a Roadmap command fails, the script prints an error and
exits non-zero. It does not fall back to another token.
Report that error. Do not retry with a personal token or `gh auth refresh`.

Run it as a separate command after `gh pr create` returns, so a failure in the
setup step never hides the PR URL. Report the PR URL and the sprint it landed in.
